            <ArticleTitle>[Syncope associated with glossopharyngeal neuralgia and parapharyngeal tumor].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>704-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The reflex-induced cardiovascular syncope is rarely associated with facial neuralgia and neck neoplasms. We report the case of a male with vasopressor and cardioinhibitor syncopes, despite the implantation of a pacemaker. Because of a glossopharyngeal neuralgia, a neoplasm of the left parapharyngeal fossae is diagnosed. The pathophysiology and the therapeutic approach is discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
